=======================================================================
Section 5
OLD_SECTION

    function isLoggedIn(){
        let status=null;
        if (sessionStorage.userProperties == undefined) {
            status = false;
        }else{
            if (sessionStorage.userProperties.auth){
                status = true;
            }
        }
    }


NEW_SECTION

    function isLoggedIn(){
        return loggedIn;
    }


REASON
isLoggedIn() had no return statement, so it always returned undefined and every protected route redirected, even for a signed-in user. It also read sessionStorage.userProperties.auth, a property of a string, which is always undefined. It now returns the app-set loggedIn flag.

=======================================================================
Section 6
OLD_SECTION
        initialize: { writable: false },
        destroy: { writable: false },
        clearCache: { writable: false }
    })


NEW_SECTION
        initialize: { writable: false },
        destroy: { writable: false },
        clearCache: { writable: false },
        loggedIn: {
            set: function(value) {
                validateBoolean(value, "SPAEngine.loggedIn property value must be a boolean");
                loggedIn = value;
            },
            get: function() {
                return loggedIn;
            }
        }
    })


REASON
Public loggedIn property: boolean-validated setter (TypeError otherwise) and a getter.

